  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.6776 acc, beating RNA-only config_002 (0.6501) by ~2.7%, confirming that the image modality contributes meaningfully. However, we have only tested ResNet50 as the image encoder. Question: Does upgrading to a stronger image encoder (ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L) further improve multimodal performance? config_008 is a clean single-variable change from config_001 (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l), isolating the effect of image encoder quality. Why this is the best next experiment: The image encoder is a high-impact design axis; ViT-L is substantially more expressive than ResNet50, and if the image branch is the bottleneck, this upgrade could yield the largest single gain available. Establishing whether ViT-L helps (or hurts) before further varying aggregation/fusion/RNA encoder ensures subsequent experiments build on the stronger backbone, making the remaining 7 experiments more efficient."
